            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go: Store.Read validates the name, walks the directories without creating anything, maps a missing root, feature directory or file to app.ErrNotFound, and re-checks the directories after the read (ErrChanged). Refusals of links and other non-regular files (ErrNotAFile), and of files above the limit (ErrTooLarge), are handled by reading one byte past review.MaxStoredBytes. The error paths all return nil bytes.",
              "engine/review/fsstore/read_test.go covers the round trip, the not-found cases with a check that nothing was created, feature and name traversal, links on the path, link/directory refusals, and the size boundary at the limit and one byte above. engine/review/fsstore/read_internal_test.go covers both race windows (a directory swapped during the read, and a file swapped for a link between Lstat and open) through injected points.",
              "Residual risk, not a finding: if a writer with access to the results directory swaps a regular file for a FIFO between Lstat and os.Open, the open could block. This needs an attacker who can already write inside the results directory, and it is untested. It is at most a hardening suggestion.",
              "engine/review/app/fakes_test.go: fakeResults.Read matches the new Results.Read contract and returns app.ErrNotFound for a missing file. The app.go changes are interface and documentation only. The Verify use case that the package comment describes is not in this candidate, so nothing in it can be checked here."
            ]
